  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "Two non-zero real numbers, \\(a\\) and \\(b,\\) satisfy \\(ab = a - b.\\) Find a possible value of \\[\\dfrac{a}{b} + \\dfrac{b}{a} - ab.\\]",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-\\dfrac12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac13\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": "2"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10-2000-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Over the common denominator \\(ab,\\) \\[\\dfrac{a}{b} + \\dfrac{b}{a} - ab = \\dfrac{a^2 + b^2 - (ab)^2}{ab}.\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(ab = a - b\\) gives \\[\\dfrac{a^2 + b^2 - (a - b)^2}{ab} = \\dfrac{2ab}{ab} = 2.\\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Combine \\(\\dfrac{a}{b} + \\dfrac{b}{a}\\) over the common denominator \\(ab\\)",
        "Replace \\(ab\\) with \\(a - b\\) inside \\((ab)^2\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
